1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,350
The cloud provider secures the building. You secure what you put inside: accounts, permissions and data.

2
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:14,950
Most cloud breaches are wrong permissions and leaked keys, not clever attacks.

3
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:25,025
Prefer short-lived credentials from roles. If you must use keys, keep them in a secrets manager and rotate them.

4
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:30,820
Turn on audit logs, so you can always see who did what, and when.

5
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:39,520
Give each identity the minimum it needs, like a cleaner who gets corridor keys, not the safe.

6
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:44,845
Deny by default, and an explicit deny always wins.

